SMART EV CHARGING STATION MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

ALGORITHM:

Step 1: Start.

Step 2: Initialize the system with three charging stations
        and set the charging rate to Rs. 10 per kWh.

Step 3: Display the main menu with the following options:
        1. Register Vehicle & Request Charging
        2. View Charging Stations
        3. View Registered Vehicles
        4. View Waiting Queue
        5. Complete Charging & Generate Bill
        6. View Charging & Billing History
        7. Exit

Step 4: Read the user's choice.

Step 5: If the user selects option 1:
        a) Enter Vehicle ID.
        b) Enter Owner Name.
        c) Enter Battery Level.
        d) Enter Battery Capacity.
        e) Validate the vehicle details.
        f) Register the vehicle.
        g) Add the vehicle to the waiting queue.

Step 6: Sort the waiting queue based on battery level.
        Vehicles with lower battery percentages
        receive higher priority.

Step 7: Check the availability of charging stations.
        a) If a station is available, assign the vehicle.
        b) Update its status to Charging.
        c) Otherwise, keep the vehicle in the waiting queue.

Step 8: If the user selects option 2:
        Display all charging stations and their status.

Step 9: If the user selects option 3:
        Display all registered vehicle details.

Step 10: If the user selects option 4:
         Display the waiting queue.

Step 11: If the user selects option 5:
         a) Enter the station ID.
         b) Check whether the station is occupied.
         c) Calculate the required charging energy.
         d) Calculate the total charging bill.
         e) Store the billing details in history.
         f) Update the battery level to 100%.
         g) Mark the station as available.
         h) Allocate the next priority vehicle.

Step 12: If the user selects option 6:
         Display charging and billing history.

Step 13: If the user selects option 7:
         Display the thank-you message.

Step 14: If the user enters an invalid choice:
         Display an error message.

Step 15: Repeat the process until the user selects Exit.

Step 16: Stop.
